    "summary": "Finger ring of silver. The front of the ring is composed of a carved piece of turquoise on the left in the shape of a leaf adjacent to a leaf made of silver below these is a small branch of red coral. There are three droplets of silver one with a stamp mark. The shank is of rectangular wire, cut at the ends to be soldered onto the bezel. The underside of the bezel is inscribed with three marks &quot;sterling&quot;, a copyright mark, and &quot;BE&quot; the maker&#039;s mark.",
